      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cavour_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cavour developed as a stop for the Chicago and North Western Railroad during the late nineteenth century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cavour_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cavour's geography makes it a prime area for pheasant hunting, contributing to its rural, community-oriented lifestyle.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
